FreeBSD port staging area for disgrace
=====================================

This directory holds the port skeleton (approach 1.B: fetch the release
tag straight from GitHub with USE_GITHUB, rebuild configure via
autoreconf). Copy its contents to audio/disgrace in the ports tree:

    cp -R dist/freebsd /usr/ports/audio/disgrace

Prerequisites and finishing steps:

1. Push the release tag the port points at (GH_TAGNAME), e.g.:

       git tag v0.1.0
       git push public v0.1.0

   The tag must exist on GitHub before the distfile can be fetched.

2. Regenerate distinfo (the placeholder in this directory cannot be
   used as-is):

       cd /usr/ports/audio/disgrace && make makesum

3. Lint and test-build:

       portlint -A
       poudriere testport -j <jail> -p <tree> audio/disgrace

Notes:

- Festival and Piper TTS support auto-detects at configure time and
  stays off in a clean poudriere build, since those dependencies are
  intentionally not declared.
- ALSA (audio/alsa-lib) is optional on FreeBSD; configure only warns
  when it is absent.
- Sibling directories dist/debian and dist/gentoo hold the Debian and
  Gentoo packaging files in the same staging fashion.
